# Conventional commits

PR titles and git commits that will squash or rebase onto `dev` or `main`
use Conventional Commits. The CI job `PR title` and the branch ruleset
reject anything else. Renovate is configured for the same shape
(`chore(deps): …`).

```
type(scope)?: description
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `chore`,
`ci`, `build`, `revert`. Optional scope is lowercase `[a-z0-9/-]+`. Optional
`!` before `:` marks a breaking change. Description is required after `: `.

Yes: `fix: isolate the Docker development stack per checkout`
Yes: `chore(deps): pin nginx docker tag to sha256:9703642`
No: `Pin nginx Docker tag to 9703642`
No: `Feat: add maps` (type is lowercase)

The first line is the type and the why, not a file list. A body is optional.
Checker: `scripts/conventional-commit-title.py`.
